--- a/Database/clan_marks/README.txt	1970-01-01 00:00:00.000000000 +0000
+++ b/Database/clan_marks/README.txt	2026-09-06 14:10:29.961523179 +0000
@@ -0,0 +1,16 @@
+Summit local clan-mark storage
+==============================
+
+The server-side legacy clan bridge reads clan marks from this directory instead
+of downloading them from /ClanContent over HTTP.
+
+Filename contract:
+    <legacy ClanMark identifier>.bmp
+
+Examples are intentionally not invented here: the exact identifier is the value
+already carried by CL.MIconCnt / clan protocol formatting and previously used as
+the basename in the legacy HTTP URL.
+
+A missing file is reported to the legacy caller as mark-read result 2, matching
+the old non-BMP/not-available path. The default mark required by clan creation is
+still unresolved and is not synthesized by this checkpoint.
diff -ruN a/Database/clan_tag_assets/README.txt b/Database/clan_tag_assets/README.txt
--- a/Database/clan_tag_assets/README.txt	1970-01-01 00:00:00.000000000 +0000
+++ b/Database/clan_tag_assets/README.txt	2026-09-06 14:15:03.996109430 +0000
@@ -0,0 +1,20 @@
+# Clan tag source assets (local server storage)
+
+Place the selectable clan-tag BMP assets here using the legacy item-code basename:
+
+    Database/clan_tag_assets/<CodeIT>.bmp
+
+When a clan leader selects a tag, the server copies that BMP to:
+
+    Database/clan_marks/<ClanMark>.bmp
+
+This replaces the legacy IIS paths:
+
+    C:\inetpub\wwwroot\brnxcontenttags\<CodeIT>.bmp
+    C:\inetpub\wwwroot\ClanContent\<ClanMark>.bmp
+
+The legacy code ignored the result of the shell `copy` command and continued the
+purchase/update flow. The SQLite/local-storage port preserves that observable
+behavior: a missing source asset does not change the existing return/message flow.
+
+No default clan-mark bitmap is synthesized by the migration.
